    summary: "Jumping from 1000Hz to 4000Hz or 8000Hz shrinks USB reporting intervals from 1.0 ms down to 0.125 ms, reducing cursor jitter on high-refresh monitors. However, saturating 8000Hz frames requires at least 1600 DPI and a clean CPU pipeline to avoid frame-time stutters and rapid battery drain.",
